.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-MAILUTILS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-mailutils ,
.Nm makemime ,
.Nm popmaildir ,
.Nm reformime ,
.Nm sendmail
.Nd BusyBox mail tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm makemime
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Nm popmaildir
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Ar MAILDIR
.Op Ar CONN_HELPER ARGS
.Nm reformime
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Nm sendmail
.Op Fl tv
.Op Fl f Ar SENDER
.Oo
.Fl amLOGIN No 4< Ns Pa user_pass.txt | Fl au Ns Ar USER Fl ap Ns Ar PASS
.Oc
.Op Fl w Ar SECS
.Op Fl H Ar 'PROG ARGS' | Fl S Ar HOST
.Op Ar RECIPIENT_EMAIL
.Ar ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the mailutils applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
Rach2 has no mail system.
.Bl -tag -width popmaildir
.It Nm makemime
Create a multipart MIME message from the specified files.
It can create messages with attachments for
.Nm sendmail .
.It Nm popmaildir
Fetch a remote mailbox into a local maildir.
.It Nm reformime
Parse a MIME message from standard input.
.It Nm sendmail
Read a message from standard input and send it.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss reformime
.Bl -tag -width "-X PROG ARGS"
.It Fl x Ar PREFIX
Extract the contents of MIME sections to files.
.It Fl X Ar PROG ARGS
Filter the contents of MIME sections through
.Ar PROG .
This must be the last option.
.El
.Pp
The compatibility options above are accepted and ignored; an unknown
option is refused.
.Ss sendmail
.Bl -tag -width "-S HOST[:PORT]"
.It Fl t
Read additional recipients from the message.
.It Fl f Ar SENDER
Use
.Ar SENDER
in
.Ql MAIL FROM:<sender> .
An empty string is permitted.
The default is the user specified by
.Fl au Ns Ar USER ,
or the name of the current user ID.
.It Fl o Ar OPTIONS
Accept compatibility options.
.Fl oi
is implied; other values are ignored.
.It Fl i
A synonym for
.Fl oi ;
it is implied and ignored.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl w Ar SECS
Set the network timeout in seconds.
.It Fl H Ar 'PROG ARGS'
Run a connection helper.
.Ev SMTP_ANTISPAM_DELAY
specifies the seconds to wait after the helper connects.
.It Fl S Ar HOST Ns Op : Ns Ar PORT
Select the server.
The default is
.Ev SMTPHOST ,
or
.Ql 127.0.0.1 .
.It Fl amLOGIN
Authenticate with AUTH LOGIN.
.It Fl amPLAIN
Authenticate with AUTH PLAIN.
.Fl amCRAM-MD5
is not supported.
.It Fl au Ns Ar USER
Set the authentication user name.
.It Fl ap Ns Ar PASS
Set the authentication password.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Fl a
options, no authentication is performed.
With
.Fl amLOGIN
but no
.Fl au
or
.Fl ap ,
the user name and password are read from file descriptor 4.
The compatibility options above are accepted and ignored; an unknown
option is refused.
.Sh HISTORY
The applet descriptions are adapted from BusyBox 1.36.1 usage text,
